_{2}-3{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-3$ times the third row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -6 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-3{R}_{3} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -6 & -1 \\\\ 3+(-3)(1) & 0+(-3)(-8) & 0+(-3)(6) \\\\ 1 & -8 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 24 & -18 \\\\ 1 & -8 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525191 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15daec48-7d83-5110-9b2c-a57ad830d293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 16 \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525164} {:answer/id #uuid "5a2cb7a3-08fb-5d81-bc68-d117ca2aaeff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525172} {:answer/id #uuid "977bc8d3-d6fa-5c85-b9e3-99ea1f4da5ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525184} {:answer/id #uuid "a0165490-acdd-5e11-a0b9-1a7348e85eb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525186} {:answer/id #uuid "b641e012-8c56-524c-ab1c-02d6ec43f004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15daec48-7d83-5110-9b2c-a57ad830d293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 16 \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525164} :answer-field/id #uuid "f50f50d7-3f10-589e-bade-734ac7312a03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525195}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eafcba40-5776-5f90-b937-69c1ed57b5e4" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}$ on $M?$" :question/worked-solution "The operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $3$ times the first row to the second row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 3+(3)(-1) & -2+(3)(5) & 7+(3)(3) \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 16 \\\\ -5 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Applying Row Operations To a Coefficients Matrix"}
